#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166423 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a8666dd9-b763-589d-8ae3-af203068f1a4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Maximum Value Given a Canonical Form on the Unit Sphere"}] :question/id #uuid "b8306278-726a-5c09-86cc-14631a6abb66" :question/math-academy-id "e-12659" :question/problem "Find the maximum value of $Q(\\mathbf{x})=2x_1^2 - 5x_2^2 +3x_3^2$ given that $\\| \\mathbf{x} \\| =1$." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that\n\n$$\nx_1^2 \\geq 0\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nx_2^2 \\geq 0\n$$\n\nSo, we have that\n\n$$\n2x_1^2 \\leq 3x_1^2, \\qquad -5x_2^2 \\leq 3x_2^2\n$$\n\nAs a result,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nQ(x) &= 2x_{1}^{2} - 5x_{2}^{2} + 3x_{3}^{2} \\\\\n&\\le 3x_{1}^{2} + 3x_{2}^{2} + 3x_{3}^{2} \\\\\n&= 3(x_{1}^{2} + x_{2}^{2} + x_{3}^{2})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that\n\n$$\n\\| \\mathbf{x} \\| = 1\n$$\n\nis equivalent to\n\n$$\nx_1^2 + x_2^2 + x_3^2 =1\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n3(x_{1}^{2} + x_{2}^{2} + x_{3}^{2}) = 3(1) = 3\n$$\n\nand, in turn,\n\n$$\nQ(\\mathbf{x}) \\leq 3\n$$\n\nSo, the value of $Q(\\mathbf{x})$ can be no greater than $3$. But before we conclude that $3$ is the maximum, we need to find a vector such that\n\n$$\nQ(\\mathbf{x}) = 3\n$$\n\nNotice that when $\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nQ(x) &= 2x_{1}^{2} - 5x_{2}^{2} + 3x_{3}^{2} \\\\\n&= 2(0)^{2} - 5(0)^{2} + 3(1)^{2} \\\\\n&= 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, given that\n\n$$\n\\| \\mathbf{x} \\| =1\n$$\n\nthe maximum value of $Q(\\mathbf{x})$ is equal to $3$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166424 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "33f7fa4d-9ac0-552a-9f3e-9e09c2ed0286" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Minimum Value Given a Canonical Form on the Unit Sphere"}] :question/id #uuid "5b4117f3-62fb-55c6-8e23-0cadcd4a2ec5" :question/math-academy-id "e-12660" :question/problem "Find the minimum value of $Q(\\mathbf{x})=5x_1^2 - 4x_2^2 - 6x_3^2$ given that $\\| \\mathbf{x} \\| =1$." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that\n\n$$\nx_1^2 \\geq 0\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nx_2^2 \\geq 0\n$$\n\nSo, we have that\n\n$$\n5x_1^2 \\geq -6x_1^2, \\qquad -4x_2^2 \\geq -6x_2^2\n$$\n\nAs a result,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nQ(x) &= 5x_{1}^{2} - 4x_{2}^{2} - 6x_{3}^{2} \\\\\n&\\ge - 6x_{1}^{2} - 6x_{2}^{2} - 6x_{3}^{2} \\\\\n&=-6(x_{1}^{2} + x_{2}^{2} + x_{3}^{2})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that\n\n$$\n\\| \\mathbf{x} \\| = 1\n$$\n\nis equivalent to\n\n$$\nx_1^2 + x_2^2 + x_3^2 =1\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n-6(x_{1}^{2} + x_{2}^{2} + x_{3}^{2}) =-6(1) =-6\n$$\n\nand, in turn,\n\n$$\nQ(\\mathbf{x}) \\geq -6\n$$\n\nSo, the value of $Q(\\mathbf{x})$ can be no smaller than $-6$. But before we conclude that $-6$ is the minimum, we need to find a vector such that\n\n$$\nQ(\\mathbf{x}) = -6\n$$\n\nNotice that when $\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nQ(x) &= 5x_{1}^{2} - 4x_{2}^{2} - 6x_{3}^{2} \\\\\n&= 5(0)^{2} - 4(0)^{2} - 6(1)^{2} \\\\\n&=-6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, given that\n\n$$\n\\| \\mathbf{x} \\| =1\n$$\n\nthe minimum value of $Q(\\mathbf{x})$ is equal to $-6$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166425 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3b2e9ac0-590b-587c-b16d-309f899c21e6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Maximum and Minimum Values of a Quadratic Form on the Unit Sphere"}] :question/id #uuid "3cec995b-8918-5c48-927e-b0807a947518" :question/math-academy-id "e-12661" :question/problem "Find the minimum value of $Q(\\mathbf{x})=x_1^2-2x_2^2-2x_3^2+2x_2x_3$ given that $\\| \\mathbf{x} \\| = 1$." :question/worked-solution "Let $A$ be the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form. Recall that:\n\n- The maximum value of $Q(\\mathbf{x})$, when $\\| \\mathbf{x} \\|=1$, is equal to the largest eigenvalue of $A{:}$\n$\\max \\{Q(\\mathbf{x}) \\: \\mid \\: \\| \\mathbf{x} \\| = 1 \\} = \\lambda_{\\textrm{max}}$\n- The minimum value of $Q(\\mathbf{x})$, when $\\| \\mathbf{x} \\|=1$, is equal to the smallest eigenvalue of $A{:}$\n$\\min \\{Q(\\mathbf{x}) \\: \\mid \\: \\| \\mathbf{x} \\| = 1 \\} = \\lambda_{\\textrm{min}}$\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix of our quadratic form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to calculate the eigenvalues of the matrix $A$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid A - λI \\mid &= 0 \\\\\n\\begin{vmatrix}1 - λ & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 - λ & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 - λ\\end{vmatrix} &= 0 \\\\\n(1 - λ)\\begin{vmatrix}-2 - λ & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2 - λ\\end{vmatrix} &= 0 \\\\\n(1 - λ)((-2 - λ)(-2 - λ) - 1) &= 0 \\\\\n(1 - λ)(λ^{2} + 4λ + 3) &= 0 \\\\\n(1 - λ)(λ + 3)(λ + 1) &= 0 \\\\\nλ &= 1,-1,-3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\min \\{Q(\\mathbf{x}) \\: \\mid \\: \\| \\mathbf{x} \\| = 1 \\} = -3\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167039 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "33f7fa4d-9ac0-552a-9f3e-9e09c2ed0286" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Minimum Value Given a Canonical Form on the Unit Sphere"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b8c9efcd-1247-5933-b64b-346934135478" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163653} {:answer/id #uuid "bca7c8f1-df96-567a-bcff-8bc7fe59518e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163654} {:answer/id #uuid "cf7ac1a3-c2a9-596d-9cdb-1dbfcef22bc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163655} {:answer/id #uuid "d49eed47-fdf5-559f-a327-b2be458ae699" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163656} {:answer/id #uuid "d7063632-c6d7-5eb1-9581-a84f5f0b9777" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163657}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8c9efcd-1247-5933-b64b-346934135478" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163653} :answer-field/id #uuid "91c8ea6e-b51f-5f03-855e-98e7ff8988c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163652}] :question/id #uuid "657b8539-11db-5516-89dc-20b2cb407f63" :question/math-academy-id "q-138019" :question/problem "Find the minimum value of $Q(x) = 5x_{1}^{2} + 3x_{2}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖ = 1$."}]}
